{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbTAXfygpsMQVdtxpHR7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015Yxa4jQ47A6qzTstq3soXz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > result.json <<'EOF'\n{\n \"candidate\": \"215d354d-44bf-45c0-9048-1df7726ee532\",\n \"family\": \"group-IV semiconductor\",\n \"tier\": \"trust\",\n \"property\": \"lattice_constant\",\n \"value\": 5.467,\n \"units\": \"angstrom\",\n \"uncertainty\": 0.05,\n \"method\": {\n  \"engine\": \"mace-torch 0.3.15 ASE calculator on CUDA GPU, ase.eos.EquationOfState (ase 3.29.0)\",\n  \"model\": \"MACE-MP-0 medium (universal MLIP trained on PBE/PBE+U MPtrj data), float64\",\n  \"protocol\": \"Static 0 K E(V) scan with uniform isotropic strain of ideal diamond-cubic Si (8-atom conventional cell; all atoms on symmetry sites, so forces are zero by symmetry). EOS fit with 3 forms (Birch-Murnaghan, Vinet, Murnaghan), 2 strain windows (+/-3% and +/-6% in a), and 2 point densities (11 and 21 points), 12 fits in total. Value = mean of the 12 fits. Checks: the 64-atom 2x2x2 supercell gives the same BM result as the 8-atom cell (5.46701 vs 5.46701 A); float32 gives 5.46704 A; mean stress at the fitted a is -0.05 GPa. Validation used the same setup on C (diamond), Ge, Cu, Al, Ag.\",\n  \"ensemble\": \"static (0 K, no MD; EOS energy-volume scan)\",\n  \"timestep_fs\": null,\n  \"n_atoms\": 8,\n  \"sim_length_ps\": null\n },\n \"flags\": [],\n \"note\": \"PREMISE: the static equilibrium lattice constant from an E(V) fit is well defined for a perfect periodic crystal. Si is in MACE-MP-0's training domain (PBE MPtrj). No timescale or size issue: no MD, and the result does not change with cell size (8 vs 64 atoms). The result is the model's static 0 K lattice constant without zero-point or thermal expansion, so it should be read as an approximation of PBE. It is not a direct prediction of the measured value. RESULT: a0 = 5.4664 A (12-fit mean; range 5.4653-5.4671 A). B0 = 88 GPa (range 86.5-89.9). VALIDATION (same model, code and protocol; experimental 300 K values as tabulated on Wikipedia 'Lattice constant', which cites Ioffe NSM, the APS/Argonne lattice-constant table, and Davey, Phys. Rev. 1925): C 3.578 vs 3.567 (+0.3%); Ge 5.720 vs 5.658 (+1.1%); Al 4.037 vs 4.046 (-0.2%); Ag 4.161 vs 4.079 (+2.0%); Cu 3.639 vs 3.597 (+1.2%; the tabulated Cu value is from a 1925 measurement and looks low compared with commonly quoted modern values, so give it little weight). These errors match the known PBE/GGA pattern: slight overestimation, worst for Ag and Ge, and about zero for Al. That pattern indicates the model reproduces its reference DFT level. The tier1.json calibration file has no lattice-constant or crystalline-density records, so it could not be used here. COMPARISON: the CODATA lattice parameter of Si is 5.431020511 A at 22.5 C in vacuum (CODATA 2022, NIST). The model value is +0.036 A (+0.65%) higher, which is within the typical PBE overestimation for Si. Thermal expansion of Si from 0 to 295 K and the zero-point correction are each of order 1e-3 A, small compared with this offset. UNCERTAINTY: numerical/fit uncertainty is +/-0.002 A (spread over EOS form, window, point density, precision and supercell). The quoted +/-0.05 A is the model-vs-experiment systematic uncertainty, estimated from the validation errors (about 1% RMS, about 0.8% for the semiconductors C and Ge). It covers the error of the MLIP and its underlying PBE functional relative to experiment. It does not cover isotopic composition, defects or impurities.\"\n}\nEOF\n./board post property_result @result.json --parent 215d354d-44bf-45c0-9048-1df7726ee532 && ./board show | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1445,"cache_read_input_tokens":39911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1445,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":